<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The sixteen small dialogs of spec.md 15b's dialogs.xrc entry:
  set_start_dlg, stop_confirm_dlg, finish_confirm_dlg,
  continue_or_new_dlg, resume_dlg, exit_running_dlg, exit_confirm_dlg
  (xrc-windows.md section B; exit_confirm_dlg added Phase 8, P8-D1),
  duplicate_ride_dlg and reopen_ride_dlg (section B, E5.4.1 mock-first —
  the two §15 rows that had no frozen window until then),
  edit_crossing_dlg, reassign_dlg, manual_deal_dlg, dnf_confirm_dlg
  (section C), about_dlg, selftest_dlg, shortcuts_dlg (section E).
  Control names are frozen; tests find them with
  FindWindowByName and tools/gen_ids.py turns them into ui/ids.py
  (R-05, R-73). Names repeat across these windows on purpose -
  plate_input, reason_input and continue_btn each appear in more than
  one - because spec.md 15b requires uniqueness only within a
  top-level window.

  Measured on wxPython 4.3.1 / wxWidgets 3.3.3:

    * wxStdDialogButtonSizer only *places* the ids its AddButton()
      recognises - wxID_OK/YES/SAVE, wxID_APPLY, wxID_NO,
      wxID_CANCEL/CLOSE, wxID_HELP/CONTEXT_HELP. Any other button is
      still created as a child of the dialog, so it resolves by name,
      but it is never added to the sizer: GetContainingSizer() is None
      and it stays at (-1,-1). void_btn, continue_btn, archive_new_btn,
      library_btn and rerun_btn therefore sit in a sibling wxBoxSizer,
      the shape entry_detail_dlg already uses.
    * <default>1</default> is honoured on wxButton, inside a std sizer
      or a box sizer; the dialog's GetDefaultItem() returns it.
      <focused>1</focused> is declared alongside it on the destructive
      confirms but could NOT be verified here: a terminal-launched,
      unbundled Python never becomes the frontmost macOS application,
      so no window takes key focus and even an explicit SetFocus()
      leaves FindFocus() at None. The functional suite has to assert
      initial focus against an activated app.
      Measured on windows-latest (Phase 10): MSW GetDefaultItem()
      follows the focused control - or the first-declared button when
      nothing is focused - and <default>1</default> alone is NOT
      honoured there. Every intended default therefore also carries
      <focused>1</focused>, which is what spec.md 13's initial-focus
      rules ask for anyway.
    * <wrap>420</wrap> is honoured on wxStaticText and is what keeps
      the three long confirm paragraphs from Fit()ing to a single
      700-940 px line. wxStaticText::Wrap() rewrites the label with
      newlines, so anything that later calls SetLabel on one of these
      has to re-wrap; they are all fixed wording, so nothing does.
    * XRC cannot give one control both a custom name and a stock id
      value: the id comes from the name attribute, and the
      name="foo=5100" form is not parsed by this build (XRCID returns
      a generated value and the window name keeps the literal "=5100").
      The canvas marks continue_btn as wxID_OK in continue_or_new_dlg
      and resume_dlg; the frozen name wins here and the affirmative
      behaviour is code-side - SetAffirmativeId(XRCID("continue_btn")).
    * wxDataViewListCtrl cannot be authored here: its XRC handler
      hard-forces the control name to "dataviewCtrl". shortcuts_list is
      a wxDataViewCtrl, whose name IS honoured.
    * wxHyperlinkCtrl needs both a label and a url; constructing it
      with neither trips a C++ assertion that aborts the interpreter,
      so gorba_link declares both.
    * <font><family>teletype</family></font> gives selftest_output a
      genuinely fixed-width face (IsFixedWidth() is True) without
      naming a font or a point size, so it still follows system
      metrics and the 90-150% zoom.
    * XRC has no minsize property for windows - only for sizeritem and
      wxSplitterWindow (wxWidgets src/xrc/xmlres.cpp SetupWindow). None
      of these dialogs has a documented minimum, so none declares a
      <size> and the sizer handler Fit()s it and applies
      SetSizeHints(). selftest_output declares a control-level <size>
      because a multi-line text area has no useful best size of its
      own.

  Recorded gap: continue_or_new_dlg and resume_dlg both put live data
  in their message line ("stopped with 1 124 crossings recorded"; the
  ride name, with the wording swapping for a crash), but the canvas
  annotates no name for either label. They are declared here as
  unnamed, empty wxStaticText and cannot be written to until the
  frozen-name registry gains a *_lbl entry for each. The same gap
  exists in delete_ride_dlg (library.xrc).

  Code-side per the canvas: edit_crossing_dlg is one resource with two
  titles - Cards > Edit Crossing and Cards > Add Crossing at Time set
  the title and prefill the fields, and void_btn is shown in edit mode
  only; every message and data label's text; selftest_output's report;
  shortcuts_list's rows, generated from the single accelerator table so
  they cannot drift.
-->
<resource>

  <!-- ============================ section B ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="set_start_dlg">
    <title>Set Start Time</title>
    <!-- R-05 requires resizable windows; the in-app text zoom (90-150%)
         cannot work in a fixed-size dialog. spec.md 13 says "dialogs
         fixed-size" - recorded conflict, resolved in favour of R-05.
         The same style is on every dialog in this file. -->
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Started at</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxDatePickerCtrl" name="start_date_picker"/>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxTimePickerCtrl" name="start_time_picker"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Lap-1 times recompute from this moment.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- Destructive confirm: Cancel is both the default and the initially
       focused control, so a reflex Enter is safe (spec.md 13,
       UX-DESKTOP 3). wxID_OK carries the canvas's verb label; the stock
       id is what keeps it on the platform-correct side. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="stop_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Stop Ride?</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>The clock stops for everyone. Riders still on course keep their laps; no cards are dealt after stop. You can continue the ride later without losing anything.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Stop ride</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="finish_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Finish Ride?</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Locks entry and computes final standings (evaluator self-test must be green). You can reopen later for corrections.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Finish ride</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- E5.4.1 mock-first (task-brief E5.4.1): File ▸ Duplicate Ride…
       previously one of the three §15 rows with no frozen window
       (commands.py's _UNAUTHORED_DIALOG sentinel). Authored mock-first:
       the control names are registered in spec.md §15b BEFORE any UI
       wiring, replacing the E1.4.1 sentinel. Duplicate copies setup +
       roster with no timing data (R-15), so it is a NON-destructive
       confirm: OK is both the default and the initially focused
       control, and a reflex Enter is safe (spec.md 13). The ride being
       duplicated is interpolated into message_lbl by the presenter
       (UX-DESKTOP §4 names the object). -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="duplicate_ride_dlg">
    <title>Duplicate Ride</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- "Duplicate "<ride name>" as a new DRAFT ride?" Written by
           the presenter; a blank label is a failed assertion. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Copies the ride's setup and full rider list — no timing data.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Duplicate</label>
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- E5.4.1 mock-first (task-brief E5.4.1): Ride ▸ Reopen Ride — the
       second §15 row that previously had no frozen window. Reopen
       moves a FINISHED ride to REOPENED for corrections (spec §3),
       which loses nothing, so this is a NON-destructive confirm: OK
       is the default and the initially focused control (spec.md 13). -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="reopen_ride_dlg">
    <title>Reopen Ride</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- "Reopen "<ride name>" for corrections?" Written by the
           presenter; a blank label is a failed assertion. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Reopen for corrections? Standings recompute on export.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Reopen</label>
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- Three buttons, so spec.md 13's order applies: ghost, secondary,
       primary left to right - Cancel, Archive & start new, Continue
       ride. The std sizer cannot do that ordering itself here because
       continue_btn cannot carry wxID_OK (see the file header), so only
       Cancel sits inside it. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="continue_or_new_dlg">
    <title>Ride Already Has Data</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- "This ride was stopped with <n> crossings recorded."
           Written by the presenter. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Continue it (keeps start time and all data) or archive and start fresh?</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="archive_new_btn">
              <label>Archive &amp;&amp; start new</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="continue_btn">
              <label>Continue ride</label>
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- Two buttons, neither of which is an id wxStdDialogButtonSizer
       places, so this dialog has no std sizer at all: library_btn is
       the secondary and continue_btn the primary, ordered left to
       right per spec.md 13. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="resume_dlg">
    <title>Resume Ride</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The ride name, and wording that swaps for a crash restart
           (session_state). Written by the presenter. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="library_btn">
              <label>Open library</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="continue_btn">
              <label>Continue ride</label>
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="exit_running_dlg">
    <title>Ride Is Running</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <!-- E5.2.3: the message line carries the frozen name message_lbl
             (spec §15b's shared name, also in continue_or_new_dlg and
             resume_dlg) so the exit path can interpolate the running
             ride's name into it; the label below is the fallback copy
             the smoke test screenshot renders, and app.py overwrites it
             with the ride-naming copy before ShowModal. -->
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="message_lbl">
          <label>Quitting won't stop the ride — it keeps timing on the wall clock, and you'll be asked to continue when you reopen.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- Three buttons per spec §3, §15 and R-51: Cancel · Finish ride
           first… · Quit-keep-running. The canvas draws only two; the
           requirements are the acceptance authority and this is missing
           functionality, not styling, so the third button stays.
           Order is §13's Ghost · Secondary · Primary.
           finish_first_btn sits outside the wxStdDialogButtonSizer
           because Realize() positions only the ids it recognises. A
           custom button placed inside it is created but left at
           (-1,-1). Cancel keeps the default so a reflex Enter is safe
           (R-76: destructive confirms focus Cancel). -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
                  <default>1</default>
                  <focused>1</focused>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxButton" name="finish_first_btn">
              <label>Finish ride first…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Quit — keep ride running</label>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- Phase 8 amendment (P8-D1/R-51/R-76): the app never exits without
       confirmation. Quitting with no ride running shows this destructive
       confirm instead of quitting outright; Cancel is both the default
       and the initially focused control, so a reflex Enter is safe. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="exit_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Quit RiverCrossing?</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Are you sure you want to quit? No ride is running.</label>
          <wrap>420</wrap>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Quit</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- ============================ section C ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="edit_crossing_dlg">
    <title>Edit Crossing</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Time</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTimePickerCtrl" name="time_picker"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="void_btn">
              <label>Void crossing…</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
                  <default>1</default>
                </object>
              </object>
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="reassign_dlg">
    <title>Reassign Plate</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- "Crossing 14:21:59 · lap credited to 45" - written by the
           presenter from the selected crossing. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="crossing_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>New plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="new_plate_input"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="manual_deal_dlg">
    <title>Deal Manual Card</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxFlexGridSizer">
          <cols>2</cols>
          <vgap>6</vgap>
          <hgap>8</hgap>
          <growablecols>1</growablecols>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Plate</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="plate_input"/>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Deals the next card from the shoe — deterministic, audit-logged.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Deal</label>
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="dnf_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Mark DNF</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The entry being marked ("212 · M. Chen"); the consequence
           beside it is fixed wording and stays in XRC. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText" name="entry_lbl">
              <label></label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>— keeps laps and cards, ranked in the DNF block. Reversible.</label>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Mark DNF</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- E7 mock-first: Void Card… confirm (spec.md §15). Authored in E7 with
       its control names registered in §15b before any UI wiring, replacing
       the E1.4.1 _UNAUTHORED_DIALOG sentinel. -->
  <object class="wxDialog" name="void_card_confirm_dlg">
    <title>Void Card</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The card being voided ("9♥ — 45 · J. Okafor"); the consequence
           beside it is fixed wording and stays in XRC. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText" name="card_lbl">
              <label></label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>— removes the card from the entry's scored hand. Audit-logged.</label>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>8</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Reason</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <option>1</option>
            <flag>wxEXPAND</flag>
            <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="reason_input"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <label>Void card</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL">
              <default>1</default>
              <focused>1</focused>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <!-- ============================ section E ============================ -->

  <object class="wxDialog" name="about_dlg">
    <title>About RiverCrossing</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The ride logo, falling back to the app icon - both supplied
           in code, so no <bitmap> is declared. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticBitmap" name="about_logo_bmp"/>
      </object>

      <!-- "RiverCrossing 1.0.0" - the version comes from the package. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText" name="version_lbl">
          <label></label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticText">
          <label>Timing &amp;&amp; poker-hand scoring for poker-run rides.</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_HORIZONTAL|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>4</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Built for GORBA —</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxHyperlinkCtrl" name="gorba_link">
              <label>gorba.ca</label>
              <url>https://gorba.ca</url>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="selftest_dlg">
    <title>Evaluator Self-Test</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <!-- The report is dot-leadered, so it only lines up in a
           fixed-width face. "teletype" asks for the system's monospace
           family rather than naming one, which keeps the control
           native and lets it follow the text zoom. -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <option>1</option>
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxTextCtrl" name="selftest_output">
          <style>wxTE_MULTILINE|wxTE_READONLY</style>
          <size>420,140</size>
          <font>
            <family>teletype</family>
          </font>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxButton" name="rerun_btn">
              <label>Run again</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="spacer">
            <option>1</option>
            <size>0,0</size>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
              <object class="button">
                <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
                  <default>1</default>
                </object>
              </object>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="shortcuts_dlg">
    <title>Keyboard Shortcuts</title>
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <option>1</option>
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxDataViewCtrl" name="shortcuts_list"/>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CLOSE">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

</resource>
